WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:01.860
- [Narrator] Principles for Success,

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:05.420
an ultra mini-series
adventure in 30 minutes,

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.360
and in eight episodes.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.956
Episode seven, be radically open-minded.

00:00:10.956 --> 00:00:12.290
(calm orchestral music)

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:15.430
Taking risks and occasionally being ruined

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:19.230
wasn't acceptable, and
neither was not taking risks,

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.860
and not having exceptional results.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:23.630
I needed an approach that would give me

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:26.670
the exceptional upside
without also giving me

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:29.050
the exceptional downside.

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:33.480
When I discovered it, it
turned out to be my holy grail.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:37.610
To get it, I needed to replace
the joy of being proven right

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:39.994
with the joy of learning what's true.

00:00:39.994 --> 00:00:41.820
(birds chirping)
(tranquil orchestral music)

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.810
This need prompted me to seek out

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.040
the most thoughtful people I could find

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:47.583
who disagreed with me.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:50.620
I didn't care about their conclusions,

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:53.430
I just wanted to see
things through their eyes,

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:56.120
and to have them see
things through my eyes,

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:58.760
so that together, we could hash things out

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:00.363
to discover what's true.

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:03.990
In other words, what I
wanted most from them

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:06.033
was thoughtful disagreement,

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:10.280
going from seeing things
through just my eyes

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:14.040
to seeing things through the
eyes of these thoughtful people

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.720
was like going from seeing
things in black and white

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.070
to seeing them in color.

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:20.180
(orchestral music builds)
(birds chirping)

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.853
The world lit up!

00:01:21.853 --> 00:01:24.101
(lion growling)

00:01:24.101 --> 00:01:25.490
(wings flapping)

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:27.540
That's when I realized that the best way

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:31.300
to go through the jungle of
life is with insightful people

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:34.210
who see things differently from me.

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:37.500
Think about the five step
process I described earlier.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.070
As I said, because we
are wired so differently,

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:42.447
not everyone can do all
the five steps well,

00:01:42.447 --> 00:01:43.400
(screaming)

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:46.070
but you don't have to do them all alone.

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:47.870
You can get help from others

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:50.270
who are good at what you're not,

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:53.790
who are wired to perceive
things you can't.

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:56.180
All you need to do is
let go of your attachment

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:59.010
to having the right answers yourself,

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.780
and use your fear of being wrong

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.498
to become open-minded
to these other views.

00:02:03.498 --> 00:02:06.110
(tranquil orchestral music)
(birds chirping)

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:09.750
In this way, you could point
out the risks and opportunities

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:12.070
that you would individually miss.

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:15.080
I found that taking this
radically open-minded approach

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:18.240
and believability
weighting people's thinking

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.880
significantly increased my probabilities

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:23.540
of making the best decisions possible.

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:26.380
This enabled me to
ascend to greater heights

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:28.510
and greater challenges.

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:30.950
In the past, I would
have always wanted to do

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:33.550
what I myself thought was best,

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:36.610
but now I sought out the
strongest independent thinkers

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:39.030
I could find, I still do.

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:42.000
There is nothing better
to be on shared mission

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.000
with extraordinary people who
can be radically truthful,

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.960
and radically transparent with each other.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:51.180
This approach led me to create a company

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:53.690
with a unique idea meritocracy,

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:58.530
operating in a unique way that
produced unique successes.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:02.730
In an idea meritocracy, you
get the best of everybody.

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:05.030
Everyone thinks independently,

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:07.070
then we work through our disagreements

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:08.870
to get at what's best.

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:12.020
However, not every opinion
is equally valuable,

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:15.510
and we had to learn to
distinguish between good ideas

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:18.230
and bad ones to get the best decisions.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.230
In other words,

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:23.030
we needed to believability
weight people's thinking.

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:25.040
But that's another story I will explain

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:26.900
in my work principles.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:30.390
Right now, there are many
wonderful opportunities

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:35.030
and dangerous risks surrounding
you that you don't see.

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:38.450
If you saw them free of
the distortions produced

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.930
by your ego or your blind spots,

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:43.890
you would be able to deal
with them more effectively.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.830
If you could acquire this ability,

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:47.980
and with practice you can,

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:50.820
you will radically improve your life.

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:54.400
In episode eight, I will conclude
our short journey together

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.630
with a few practical thoughts

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:59.140
so that you can begin your own journey

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:01.213
toward whatever you want.

